  "area": "discovery",
  "description": "AGSC-06-40: the Link header of the home page carries the FAIR Signposting Level 1 links (signposting.org/FAIR, read 2026-10-29): cite-as exactly once (the first related[] cite-as link in href order, else the Bundle IRI), two type links (https://schema.org/Dataset then https://schema.org/AboutPage), describedby for the discovery document and for /graph.jsonld, item for the graph files and the chunks, license when the node has a licence URL (AGSC-06-44), and linkset for the discovery document. The values are compared as a set of {href, rel, type} (the order and the folding of the values into one field or several are not asserted, and the targets on the node are root-relative while cite-as and license are absolute). Three nodes: public with a DOI as cite-as and a versioned licence URL; public with the defaults (the Content Use Terms, /legal/ emitted); restricted (no item link). The validator part: given a URL whose / response lacks the describedby link, validate-wellknown reports a warning under AGSC-E202, because the header is a SHOULD in AGSC-06-25. Derived by hand from the rule.",
